#an out-of-synch disassembly.
#.($115)Assemble
#The \bAssemble\r command pops up a box to allow you to enter
#(patch) a new instruction into
#code
#memory at the currently
#highlighted location.  After you enter a new instruction,
#the highlight bar will move down automatically to the
#location following that new instruction to allow you to enter
#several instructions in succession.
#.sp 1
#While the Assembler input box is visible, you can also move
#the highlight bar up or down one line using the arrow keys
#('\x19' and '\x18').
#.sp 1
#When entering an instruction, symbolic information may be used.
#This includes the ability to define a new label at the current
