#.ti -3
#\b%rs1-8051 Modular Emulator:\r
#.sp 1
#The %rs2 \b%rs1-8051 Modular\r emulator consists of an
#8051-architecture-specific emulator base unit,
#attached to a small probe card (pod) via an umbilical cable.
#The probe card, which contains the device being emulated,
#inserts into the socket for the device in your target
#development system.  Many probe cards are available, supporting a
#wide variety of 8051
#CMOS, NMOS, ROM, EPROM or ROMless devices.
#The emulator base unit connects to the
#host PC (personal computer) via a standard RS-232-C serial
#communications link operating at 115.2K baud.
#.sp 1
#The \b%rs1-8051 Modular\r emulator is a
#high-performance, full-featured, economical,
#small profile/footprint emulator supporting
#full probe card interchangeability.
#.sp 1
#.ti -3
#\b%rs1-PE Integrated Emulator:\r
#.sp 1
#The %rs2 \b%rs1-PE Integrated\r emulator consists of
#a single unit containing both
#the emulator base electronics and the probe card (pod) electronics.
#The entire unit (about the size of a PC mouse),
#inserts into the socket for the device in your target
#development system.
#\b%rs1-PE Integrated\r emulators are available for a limited number of
#8051 family derivative devices.
#The emulator unit connects to the
#host PC via a standard RS-232-C serial
#communications link operating at 57.6K baud.
#.sp 1
#The \b%rs1-PE Integrated\r emulators are
#high-performance, full-featured, economical,
#tiny profile/footprint emulators;  each
#emulator is \udedicated\r to a particular 8051 family derivative
#device.
#.sp 1
#.ti -3
#\b%rs1-HSM Modular Emulator\r:
#.sp 1
#The %rs2 \b%rs1-HSM Modular\r emulator supports the
#Dallas Semiconductor HSM (High Speed Micro) family of 8051-compatible
#devices.
#The \b%rs1-HSM Modular\r emulator consists of a small
#emulator base unit,
#attached to a small probe card (pod) via an umbilical cable.
#The probe card, which contains the device being emulated,
#inserts into the socket for the device in your target
#development system.  Probe cards are available supporting the entire
#Dallas HSM family.
#The emulator base unit connects to the
#host PC (personal computer) via a standard RS-232-C serial
#communications link operating at 57.6K baud.
#.sp 1
#The \b%rs1-HSM Modular\r emulator is an advanced,
#high-performance, full-featured, economical,
#small profile/footprint emulators supporting
#full probe card interchangeability within the Dallas HSM family.
#.in -3 }
