#.($356)Probe Clip Assembly
#The Probe Clip Assembly can be installed on the probe card
#at your option.  It has:
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#.in +4 {
#.ti -4
#A)^^Seven (7)
#Trace Input signal lines
#.ti -4
#B)^^One (1) Break-Point Input line
#.ti -4
#C)^^One (1) Trace Trigger Output line
#.ti -4
#D)^^Four (4) Ground lines
#.in -4 }
#.in -2 }
#.sp 1
#The 14-pin female connector plugs in with Pin 1 (marked on the
#connector body) oriented to the silkscreened \bB\r at the corner
#of the male header on the probe card (see following diagram).
#.sp 1
#\bTrace^Inputs\r:^^The probe clip trace
#input signal lines are inputs to a 74LS245 device (Model 200/400)
#or a 74HC-type device (PE) on the probe card.
#You can use these seven probe clip input lines to select (capture)
#any TTL-level signal and record its state, once each CPU (bus) cycle,
#in the Trace Buffer during emulation.
#You can view the input signal line levels in
#the \l($210)View^Trace\m menu in three
#different \l($215)Probes\m display formats.
#.sp 1
#\bBreak-Point^Input\r:^^This signal connects
#to a 74ACT245 device (Model 200/400) or a 74HC-type device (PE)
#on the probe card.  Normally, the Break-Point
#Input is pulled up (high) with a pull-up resistor:
#2K ohm (Model 200/400) or 10K ohm (PE).
#Pulling this input low during emulation causes the emulator
#to break (stop) emulation.
#The Break-Point Input is active \ulow\r and \umust\r remain
#active (low) for at least one (1) instruction (machine) cycle.
#.sp 1
#\bTrace^Trigger^Output\r:^^This signal connects
#to a 74ACT245 device (Model 200/400) or a 74HC-type device (PE)
#on the probe card.
#The Trace Trigger Output signal is normally high and will strobe
#low (active) when the executing program passes through a
#\l($164)Trace-On-Point\m address (see \l($151)Break^Menu\m).
#The Trace Trigger Output remains active for a minimum of
#one (1) CPU (bus) cycle.
#.sp 1
#The Probe Clip Assembly:
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#.ba {
# ________________________________________________________
#|                         | Orientation of Header and    |
#|                         | Silkscreened Labels as They  |
#|   Schematic of Male     | Actually Appear on a Probe   |
#|  Header on Probe Card   | Card                         |
#|=========================|==============================|
#|   G  G  G  6  4  2  0   |                              |
#|  ---------------------  |     ---------------------    |
#| | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | |    | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | 0 |
#| | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | |    | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | 1 |
#|  ---------------------  |     ---------------------    |
#|   B  T  G  NC 5  3  1   |      B  T           CLIPS    |
#|-------------------------|------------------------------|
#|   1  3  5  NC G  T  B   |     CLIPS           T  B     |
#|  ---------------------  |     ---------------------    |
#| | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | |  1 | o  o  o  o  o  o  o |   |
#| | o  o  o  o  o  o  o | |  0 | o  o  o  o  o  o  o |   |
#|  ---------------------  |     ---------------------    |
#|   0  2  4  6  G  G  G   |                              |
#|_________________________|______________________________|
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
# ____________________________________________________
#|         |                |Label   |                |
#|         |                |Printed | Color of       |
#|Schematic|                |on Probe| Corresponding  |
#|Marking  |  Pin Function  |Card    | Probe Clip     |
#|=========|================|========|================|
#| 0 - 6   | Probe Clips    | CLIPS  | All same color |
#|         | (Trace Inputs) |        | (but not:      |
#|         |                |        |  Green         |
#|         |                |        |  Yellow or     |
#|         |                |        |  Black     )   |
#|---------|----------------|--------|----------------|
#| B       | Break Input    | B      | Green          |
#|---------|----------------|--------|----------------|
#| T       | Trigger Output | T      | Yellow         |
#|---------|----------------|--------|----------------|
#| G       | Ground         | ---    | Black          |
#|---------|----------------|--------|----------------|
#| NC      | Not Connected  | ---    | ---            |
#|_________|________________|________|________________|
#.in -2 }
