#each symbol.
#.sp 1
#If the symbol name is preceded by a plus sign ('+') that symbol was
#read from the $MODEL file during \b%rs1\r initialization.
#If the symbol
#name is preceded by an asterisk ('*') that symbol is defined as a
#global (public) symbol.  Note that all symbols read from the $MODEL
#file are treated as global (public) symbols.
#.sp 1
#The value of a symbol can be displayed in various formats,
#which can be chosen using the \l($479)Value^Formats\m options.
#.sp 1
#As you scroll through the Symbol Windows, if the currently highlighted
#item is a scalar or a pointer, you will see the \bEnter:Change\r
