#\l($5)Configure|Emulator|Execute\m command.
#.sp 1
#If you want the emulator's
#code
#memory to be initialized to the value every time the
#emulator is used you must save it to the $MISC
#file using the \l($77)Configure|Save|Save\m
#command.
#.($465)Dump
#You can use the \bDump\r command to write a block of external data
#memory to a disk file.  The block will be written in the same format
#that the data is displayed on screen.
