#in the COP8 Debug Module or EPU.)
#.sp 1
#The \bWatch\r command calls a pulldown menu which gives
#you access to \l($384)Watch^Window\m commands.  You may
#\l($62)Add\m, \l($63)Delete\m, \l($486)Clear\m, \l($487)Save\m
#or \l($488)Load\m Watch \l($244)Expressions\m.
#.($486)Configure|Windows|Watch|Clear
#The \bWatch|Clear\r command clears all Watch \l($244)Expressions\m
#from the \l($384)Watch^Window\m.
#.($487)Configure|Windows|Watch|Save
#The \bWatch|Save\r command allows you to save your
#\l($384)Watch^Window\m
#setup (all Watch \l($244)Expressions\m)
#to a file which can then be loaded at another time (using the
#\l($488)Watch|Load\m command).
#.($488)Configure|Windows|Watch|Load
#The \bWatch|Load\r command allows you to load a previously
#saved (via \l($487)Watch|Save\m) \l($384)Watch^Window\m
#setup (all Watch \l($244)Expressions\m).
#.($489)Search
#The \bSearch\r command lets you search a block a memory
#for a value (or values).  When you select the \bSearch\r command
#a dialog box will pop up to prompt for the search type
#(Match or Mismatch), the address
#range to search and the pattern to search for in that range.
#.sp 1
#The search pattern may contain one or many \l($244)expressions\m up to
#a total typed length of about 80 characters.  If multiple
#expressions are needed, they must be separated by commas (',') or
#spaces (' ').
#ASCII literals must be quoted (e.g, use 'A' to put the ASCII
#value of 'A' in memory and "ab" to put the ASCII values for 'a'
#and 'b' in memory).
#.($490)Notebook/Laptop (LCD) Default
#The \bNotebook/Laptop (LCD) Default\r command sets up video colors and
#other display attributes suitable for LCD monitors used in
#notebook and laptop computers.  The supplied binary file
#\l($250)$CLRL$\m contains these color definitions.
#.($491)Bin Sort Order
#The \bBin\r command sets the sort order for bins in the
