#.($530)Configure|Windows|Highlight
#(Note:  The \bHighlight\r command is not available
#in the COP8 Debug Module or EPU.)
#.sp 1
#The \bHighlight\r command toggles whether or not the host software
#will highlight values which change from one emulation cycle
#(\l($96)Run\m) to the next.
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#.in +6 {
#.ti -6
#On:^^^The host software will highlight Main Screen Window values
#(contents) which change from one emulation cycle to the next.
#This "changed-value highlighting" applies to the following Main
#Screen Windows:
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#.ba {
#   Watch Window
#   Register Window
#*  Stack Window
#*  Code Memory Windows #1 - #n
#*  Internal Data Memory Windows #1 - #n
#.sp 1
#      * indicates a Memory Dump Window
#.ea }
#.in -2 }
#.sp 1
#In the Memory Dump Windows, when the data is being displayed in both
#hex and ASCII, the host software highlights both interpretations
#(i.e., hex byte and ASCII character) when a value changes.
#.sp 1
#If a window has a \l($59)current-position^expression\m associated
#with it (e.g., "SP" for the Stack Window),
#the host software highlights the \l($59)current-position^indicator\m
#character when the current-position expression changes and the
#current position is visible in the window.
#Additionally, when the current-position expression changes,
#the software highlights the actual current-position expression value
#displayed on the right side of the upper border of the window.
#.sp 1
#\b"Previous Value" Snapshots\r
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#In order to perform "changed-value highlighting", the host software
#takes a snapshot of each active window's data just before you perform
#an emulation cycle (\l($96)Run\m:  Step, Go or Reset).  It is this
#snapshot that the software compares the current values against in
#order to highlight those values which have changed.  The size of the
#snapshot depends on the type of window:
#.in +2 {
#.sp 1
#\bRegister Window\r
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#The snapshot consists of the values in
#all SFRs and other "special" registers, regardless of what is currently
#visible in the Register Window and whether the Register Window
#is even active (displayed).
#.in -2 }
#.sp 1
#\bWatch Window\r
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#The snapshot consists of the values of
#all Watch Expressions, whether they are currently visible in the
#Watch Window or not.
#.in -2 }
#.sp 1
#\bAll Other Main Screen Windows\r
#.sp 1
#.in +2 {
#The host software only snaps what is currently visible in the window
#at the time the snapshot is taken.
#.in -2 }
#.in -2 }
#.in -2 }
#.sp 1
#.ti -6
#Off:^^The host software will not highlight Main Screen Window values
#(contents) which change from one emulation cycle to the next.
#Additionally, the host software does not take any "Previous Value"
#snapshots (see above) before beginning emulation.
#.in -6 }
#.in -2 }
