#start an automatically repeated cycle of single-step emulations.
#You can single-step either by machine \l($272)Instruction\m
#or by HLL source \l($541)Line\m.
#This is not real-time
#emulation, since the system executes only one instruction
#(or the instructions generated for one HLL source line),
#then breaks and updates the Main Screen Windows, then continues.
#.sp 1
#You stop a \bSlow^Motion\r emulation by pressing the \bEsc\r key.
#.sp 1
#You control the speed of operation of the \bSlow Motion\r emulation.
#The default delay between each
#repetition of the cycle is 500 milliseconds (1/2 second).
#You can increase the delay (go slower) by pressing the
#minus key, \b-\r.
#You can decrease the delay (go faster) by pressing the
#plus key, \b+\r.
#The Status Window shows the current delay time in the \bState:\r
#field.
#When you change speed, note that only one change increment is allowed
#per single-step.
#.sp 1
